  "provenance": "prospective",
  "question_text": "Top-band print-through: control strip at the baseline's 3 wall loops",
  "hypothesis": "The ripples in the top band of every RIFT tile (photos IMG_1475, 1484, 1496, 1503; 4 Nov) are 15% grid infill printing through the face: the slice of the 10-inch baseline switches from solid to grid infill at 203.6 mm, where the cavity roof closes, and keeps grid about 0.8 mm behind the face's outer wall, under 3 walls, to 219.2 mm, the band's height in the photos. The dashes sit at that switch.",
  "prediction": "The strip reproduces the full tiles' top band: diagonal stripes and a row of dashes from about 203.6 mm (11.6 mm above the strip's base). If it prints clean, the band needs the full tile (its height or print time) and E-027 can't be judged against it.",
  "why_this_test": "A strip of the top 28 mm keeps the geometry and toolpath that make the band, at a fraction of a full tile's 5 h 47 m. Wall loops apply to the whole plate, so the control prints on its own plate.",
